      "title": "Read me first",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## 14 · Face refine of a finished take\n\n**Why:** MiniMax H3 draws faces poorly when the head is a small part of the\nframe — a group at a table, a wide shot — even at 720p. This graph tracks the\nface on every frame, crops it so it fills a 768 px canvas, lets H3 redraw it\nthere (as a close-up, which H3 does well) with partial denoise, and stitches it\nback with a soft mask. The picture outside the face and the soundtrack are kept.\n\n**Needs:**\n- [ComfyUI-H3-FaceRefine](https://github.com/Carasibana/ComfyUI-H3-FaceRefine) — the face nodes;\n- [ComfyUI-H3-NativeAudioLock](https://github.com/Shrek3OnVH5/MiniMax-H3-NativeAudio-MusicVideo-Workflow)\n  (copy its `custom_nodes/ComfyUI-H3-NativeAudioLock` folder into yours) — holds\n  the clip's own sound fixed while the face is redrawn, so the lips keep matching\n  the speech;\n- [Impact Pack](https://github.com/ltdrdata/ComfyUI-Impact-Pack) with its Subpack\n  (registers the detector folders) and\n  [VideoHelperSuite](https://github.com/Kosinkadink/ComfyUI-VideoHelperSuite).\n\n**Use:**\n1. Paste the take's path into **1. The take to refine** — a file from\n   `clips/NN_name/video/` of your project.\n2. Paste the same clip's **prompt** into the H3 node (the takes gallery shows it\n   in a take's settings) and load the character's **reference** picture.\n3. Queue. The result lands in `output/vig_h3_face_refine/`. Copy it into the\n   clip's `video/` folder and it appears in the takes gallery beside the\n   original — compare the two in **A/B**, and put the better one on the timeline.\n\n**The dial is denoise** (the scheduler, 0.40). It is scaled per frame by face\nsize: small faces are redrawn, large ones only touched. Too low — nothing\nchanges; too high — the head drifts against the body. Steps must match the\nTurbo LoRA (4 here). A take with several people: pick the face with `select`\non the tracker (largest, left-most, closest to a point …) and run once per face.\n\nBuilt on the Auto Select example of ComfyUI-H3-FaceRefine —\nMIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Carasibana. Their README explains every dial.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
